  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "13. Terrain",
    "ruleNumber": "13.08",
    "summary": "For a ranged attack, check every model in the target unit. Being within a terrain area qualifies a model that has **INFANTRY**, **BEASTS** or **SWARM**. So does a terrain feature or [Obscuring](vsdata:core-rule/obscuring) terrain preventing the attacking model from seeing it in full. Grant **Benefit of Cover** when all the target’s models qualify. This worsens the attack’s **BS** by 1. **[[IGNORES COVER]](vsdata:weapon-ability/ignores-cover)** bypasses it. [Stealth](vsdata:core-ability/stealth), [Indirect Shooting](vsdata:core-rule/indirect-shooting) and [Smokescreen](vsdata:core-rule/smokescreen) have their own ways to grant it. Under [Hit Rolls](vsdata:core-rule/hit-rolls), an unmodified 6 is a critical hit before comparing the roll with **BS**.",
